      "text": "The definition of the absolute value function tells us that:\n$$|x+1| = \\begin{cases} x+1 ~,& x \\geq -1 \\\\ -(x+1) ~,& -1 < x < 1 \\\\ -(x+1) ~,& x \\leq -1 \\end{cases}$$\nTherefore, the allowed values for $x$ are $x \\in [-1,1].$\nNow, consider the combinations of the absolute values:\nIf $x < -1$ then the expression is:\n$~ (-1)(x-1) - (x+1)(-1) = x - 1 + x + 1 = 2x ~,$\nIf $x = 1$ the expression is $2(1)$,\nand if $-1 \\leq x < 1$ the expression is\n$(x+1) - (x-1) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x + 1 - x + 1 = 2,$\nAll in all, the range is $x \\in [0,2].$The answer is: [0,2]",
