      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve for the range of $$G(x) = |x + 1| - |x - 1|,$$ note that by the definition of absolute value, we have \\begin{align*}\n|x + 1| &= \\begin{cases} -x - 1, \\quad &x < -1\\\\0, &-1 \\leq x < 1 \\\\x + 1, \\quad &x \\geq 1\\end{cases}.\n\\end{align*}\nSimilarly, we have \\begin{align*}\n|x - 1| &= \\begin{cases} -x + 1, \\quad &x < 1\\\\0, &1 \\leq x < 2 \\\\x - 1, \\quad &x \\geq 2\\end{cases}. \\end{align*}\nTherefore, we have \\begin{align*}\nG(x) &= |x + 1| - |x - 1| \\\\\n&= \\left[ |x - 1| = -(x - 1), x < 1 \\right] - \\left[ |x - 1| = x - 1, x \\geq 1 \\right] \\\\\n&= \\left[ -(x - 1), x < 1 \\right] - \\left[ x - 1, x \\geq 1 \\right]\\\\\n&= \\left[ -x + 1, x < 1 \\right] - \\left[ x - 1, x \\geq 1 \\right]\\\\\n&= \\begin{cases} 1 - x, &x < 1\\\\1, &x = 1\\end{cases}.\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, the range of the function $$G(x) = |x + 1| - |x - 1|= \\boxed{[1, 1 - x).}.$$The final answer is: 1",
